## Goal
Make `SetUnwrap` (the editor of the `unwrap` and `unwrap_skip_openers` keys in the rules file) non-destructive: preserve comments on the old keys, tolerate a column-0 comment inside the skip list, and keep CRLF line endings. Also cover the 503 path of the settings endpoint (DEV-48).

## Problems
None recorded in the session slice. From the diff: removing the old keys dropped their comments, a column-0 comment inside the list ended the item run early, and the inserted lines always used LF, so CRLF files got mixed line endings.

## Decision
- Detect the line ending once (CRLF if the text contains it) and use it for all inserted lines, including the newline added when the last kept line lacks one.
- While dropping the old key blocks, collect comments inside the list into a `loose` list and re-emit them above the new keys. A trailing comment on a key line is re-attached to the rewritten key line.
- If the key is no longer written (default value), its trailing comment becomes a standalone line, so nothing is lost.
- A column-0 comment is treated as part of the list only when a list item follows it, so an unrelated comment after the list is not swallowed.
- Added tests for comment retention, the column-0 comment, and CRLF (with and without a final newline). Added a settings test: when the rules file is offloaded, POST to `/api/settings/unwrap` returns 503, triggers a download, leaves the file untouched, and GET reports `editable: false`.

